# Where `op run` finds the release signing secrets (see docs/release-signing.md).
#
# THIS FILE HOLDS NO SECRETS AND IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. Every value is an
# `op://` reference — a vault path, resolved by the 1Password CLI against the
# signed-in account at the moment `just release-apk` runs. Committing the
# references is what stops the next person guessing which item the key is in;
# committing the values would be the thing this whole arrangement exists to
# prevent.
#
# `FILEFIN_STORE_FILE` is deliberately absent: it is a path to a temp file that
# does not exist until tool/release-apk.sh has fetched the keystore, so the
# script exports it rather than 1Password resolving it.
FILEFIN_STORE_PASSWORD=op://Private/FileFin Android signing/store password
FILEFIN_KEY_ALIAS=op://Private/FileFin Android signing/key alias
FILEFIN_KEY_PASSWORD=op://Private/FileFin Android signing/key password
